# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~1.6GB, and machine-specific. requirements.txt is what reproduces it — that
# is the entire reason the versions there are pinned. Committing this would
# also exceed GitHub's 100MB per-file hard limit on torch's compiled libraries
# and abort the push partway.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and datasets  --  READ BEFORE REMOVING THESE LINES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two separate reasons, both important:
#
#   1. Size. Checkpoints and image datasets are large binaries. Git stores every
#      version forever, so a repo that tracks them grows without bound and can
#      never be shrunk without rewriting history.
#
#   2. Ownership. Model Doctor is a personal project, but detection models and
#      datasets frequently originate from work under an employer's ownership.
#      Publishing those to a public repository is a confidentiality problem that
#      cannot be undone: a pushed file stays in history and stays fetchable even
#      after it is deleted. This repository is currently private, but flipping it
#      to public exposes the entire history at that instant.
#
# If you ever intend to version weights deliberately, use Git LFS and confirm
# the data is yours to publish. Do not simply delete these lines.
#
# The contents are ignored, but a .gitkeep is allowed through so that a fresh
# clone still has the directory layout the health check expects.
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
datasets/*
!datasets/.gitkeep

# Weight formats, ignored anywhere in the tree — not just the folders above.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets  --  never commit these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.envrc
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
.pypirc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recreated by config.ensure_output_dirs() and by any inference run.
results/
runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so

# Packaging
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Test and coverage
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.cover
.hypothesis/

# Type checkers and linters
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
cython_debug/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints

# Logs
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling — machine-local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer Claude Code permissions. The `.local.json` suffix is the
# convention for settings that are not shared; `.claude/settings.json` would be
# the file to commit if a project-wide config is ever wanted.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
